Source: pg-local-cache
Section: database
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Ruohang Feng <rh@vonng.com>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), postgresql-all (>= 217~)
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Rules-Requires-Root: no
Homepage: https://github.com/profundium/pg_local_cache

Package: postgresql-PGVERSION-pg-local-cache
Architecture: any
Provides: postgresql-pg-local-cache
Depends: ${postgresql:Depends}, ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: Transaction-aware primary-key row cache for PostgreSQL PGVERSION
 pg_local_cache keeps bounded whole-row entries in PostgreSQL shared memory and
 accelerates supported primary-key reads while preserving PostgreSQL as the
 source of truth. It targets one configured database and one writable primary.
 The module requires shared_preload_libraries and a PostgreSQL restart before
 its cache workers and SQL fast path can be used.
